@startuml
title FootInTheDoor - Target-to-Actionable-Profile Workflow
skinparam shadowing false

|Sanbor user|
start
:Select a company from the existing target list;
:Provide Sanbor capability context\nand known target information;

|Research process (manual or assisted)|
:Identify the relevant business unit,\nfacility, location, or program;
:Gather permitted evidence about company\nneeds, relevant people, and possible entry points;
:Assess company fit against Sanbor's\nproducts and capabilities;
:Identify decision-makers and influencers\nacross relevant functions;
:Document practical entry points and\nverify business contact details where available;
:Review buying signals and explain\npossible relevance to Sanbor's solutions;

if (Evidence of an explicit supplier search?) then (yes)
  :Label the finding as a confirmed supplier-search\nopportunity with supporting source and date;
  note right
    Confirmation concerns the documented search.
    Sanbor eligibility, relevance, and whether it is
    still open must be checked separately.
  end note
else (no)
  if (Evidence of a potential business need?) then (yes)
    :Label as a potential need;\nexplain inference and uncertainty;
  else (no)
    :Record no supported opportunity signal found;
  endif
endif

:Attach sources, dates, verification status,\nand information gaps to findings;
:Recommend priority with rationale,\nan outreach angle, and next steps\nwhere evidence supports them;

|FootInTheDoor platform|
:Present the integrated company profile\nand expose supporting evidence;

|Sanbor user|
:Review fit, contacts, entry points,\nopportunity status, and suggested actions;
if (Enough evidence to pursue?) then (yes)
  :Choose outreach steps outside the platform;
else (no)
  :Defer the target or request further research;
endif
:Provide feedback to refine future results;
stop
@enduml
